 "M17:Create a Resume & Cover Letter": "<div class=\"study-note english-note\"><div class=\"revision-banner\"><strong>ENGLISH SUCCESS · M17</strong><span>PROJECT BRIEF</span></div><h2>Create a Resume &amp; Cover Letter</h2><h3>Purpose and audience</h3><p>Prepare truthful documents for a selected role. Agree the audience, scope and review arrangements before beginning. Use a clearly labeled sample case or an authorized real task.</p><h3>Required deliverables</h3><ol><li>A role-requirements list matched with your actual evidence.</li><li>A concise resume following the employer&#x27;s instructions.</li><li>A tailored cover letter and a consistency check of names, dates and claims.</li></ol><h3>Working process</h3><ol><li>Plan your response and select relevant evidence.</li><li>Create an original draft or actual performance record as the task requires.</li><li>Request specific feedback, revise and keep a reflection on your personal contribution.</li></ol><h3>Assessment rubric</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Criterion</th><th>Evidence to review</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Purpose and organization · 25%</td><td>Clear audience, logical sequence and an appropriate response to the brief.</td></tr><tr><td>Language and communication · 30%</td><td>Meaning, appropriate register, understandable delivery or clear writing, with task-relevant accuracy.</td></tr><tr><td>Evidence and integrity · 25%</td><td>Supported claims, source credit, truthful contribution and authorized use.</td></tr><tr><td>Feedback and revision · 20%</td><td>Visible response to feedback and a specific plan for improvement.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>This rubric supports practical review; a written quiz cannot automatically grade a speech, listening performance or original portfolio. Arrange actual reviewer feedback through the agreed course process.</p><h3>Submission and reflection</h3><p>Keep labeled files, sources, feedback and revised versions. Obtain permission for recording other people and share only through approved arrangements. State permitted assistance and your personal contribution. The app does not record audio or upload these project files; confirm submission and official completion requirements in the TIH Learning Hub.</p></div>",
